Z||000000||Carrolles||02-12-2001||07:38 AM||||Does anyone know if Dupli-color or anyone else makes touch up paint in spray cans to match my red 85GT (both the red and the med. grey) and my light grey metallic 85SE?<P>The Helms manual says the paint code is found on a Body lable found on the bulkhead behind the headlights in the engine compartment.  I don't have headlights in my engine compartment, do you?  Are the paint codes in the RPO lable on the inner front left fender?<P><BR>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-12-2001||09:48 AM||||Correct on the RPO label, the paint code is on the bottom and starts with WA-.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||05:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>Correct on the RPO label, the paint code is on the bottom and starts with WA-.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>also...if you have 2 tone, there will be 2 numbers with a WA____<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Vlad||02-13-2001||01:52 AM||||Lets say we are in trouble....<P>I have gray/lt.gray 85 GT and there was no place where I could find match for my paint. <BR>Some people say that there is no perfect match for this paint made for GM.<P>So I don't know what can be done about that...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-13-2001||08:15 AM||||Ed Parks told me that FOCOA is the only place that he knows of that has touch up spray paint for our Fieros.||||reg||1
